WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.183 --> 00:00:02.160
- I was stuck in an elevator for two hours

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.940
and I had to make the whole time.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.040
But I don't blame them, 'cause
one time I turned into a dog

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.010
and they helped me.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.008
Thank you.

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:12.022
- (chuckles) Short but pointless

00:00:12.022 --> 00:00:15.630
(whimsical music plays)

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.170
Hey Legal Eagles! It's time
to think like a lawyer.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.150
And today, we are covering
one of my favorite,

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.890
let's say, guilty pleasure movies.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.970
I have a soft spot in my
heart for Ghostbusters 2.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.130
I know the first Ghostbusters movie

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.300
is basically a perfect movie.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.720
That being said, gun to my head,

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.840
I think I might actually
watch Ghostbusters 2 instead

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.270
if they're both on TV.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.510
I think Ghostbusters 2 was just on cable

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:40.910
more often as a kid.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:44.360
I can probably still
quote most of the scenes

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.778
from The Scoleri Brothers' trial.

00:00:46.778 --> 00:00:47.974
- (mimicking film
characters) Your witness.

00:00:47.974 --> 00:00:49.374
- (mimicking film
characters) Yes, we're back.

00:00:49.374 --> 00:00:51.830
- (mimicking film characters)
We be fast and they be slow.

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.670
- So as always, be sure to comment

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:54.910
in the form of an objection

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:57.040
which I'll either sustain or overrule.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.540
And stick around until
the end of the video

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.350
where I give the court
scene from Ghostbusters 2

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.453
a grade for legal realism.

00:01:03.453 --> 00:01:07.874
So without further ado, let's
dig in to Ghostbusters 2.

00:01:07.874 --> 00:01:10.980
(whimsical music)

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.260
- [Devin] Now it occurs
to me that you probably

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:14.550
need some background for this court scene.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.430
In Ghostbusters 2, there
have been a resurgence

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.820
of ghost and slime-related incidents

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:21.750
and the Ghostbusters are investigating

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.060
a river of supernatural
slime that is flowing

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:26.440
throughout lower Manhattan.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.790
In the course of investigating
this river of slime,

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:31.410
the Ghostbusters have been
arrested by the New York police

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.490
for basically drilling a giant hole

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.750
in the middle of 5th Avenue and causing

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:38.880
an enormous power outage
for most of the New Yorkers

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:39.780
on Manhattan.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.960
So, with that preface,
let's go to the court scene

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.713
in Ghostbusters 2.

00:01:44.713 --> 00:01:48.402
(bus engine roaring)

00:01:48.402 --> 00:01:49.720
- [Judge] Before we begin this trial,

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:51.460
I wanna make one thing very clear.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:54.250
- All right, so right off
the bat, we have some actual

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.560
legal realism, which is
interesting for a change.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.840
This is the famous New York Supreme Court.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:02.149
It's on Center Street in lower Manhattan.

00:02:02.149 --> 00:02:06.000
This is actually the place
where New York courts

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.250
deal with a lot of criminal infractions.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.440
Now the New York Supreme
Court is not to be confused

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.160
with the US Supreme Court
or the Supreme Court

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:14.100
of many states.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.700
For some reason, New York is
really weird in that they call

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.660
the lower trial court the
Supreme Court even though

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.530
it is the equivalent of
what most states call

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:25.430
the Superior Court or
the lowest trial court.

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:26.940
The highest court in New York is called

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.500
the Court of Appeals, for some reason.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.160
Maybe that's just a bit of
trivia that only I care about

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:33.690
but it's a super weird way
for the New York courts

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:36.450
to name their courts and
it's very counterintuitive.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.020
But it is actually the place where

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:42.960
this particular criminal trial
would probably take place.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.830
- Law does not recognize
the existence of ghosts,

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:47.490
and I don't believe in them either.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:48.323
- Right.

00:02:48.323 --> 00:02:49.730
- Don't wanna hear a lot of malarkey about

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.810
goblins and spooks and demons.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.387
We're gonna stick to
the facts in this case

00:02:53.387 --> 00:02:56.820
and leave the ghost stories
to the kiddies, understood?

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.720
- Now, that is absolutely
true that the courts

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:04.720
will not recognize ghosts in
any particular criminal trial.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.810
That being said, there
was a New York case where

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.901
a house being haunted was, in fact,

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:13.300
a very important part
of the facts and issues

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.260
- [Devin] called Stambovksy v. Ackley

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:18.670
where someone tried to get
out of the sale of a house or,

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.750
particularly, purchasing
a house because the house

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:24.510
was well-known in the
community to be haunted.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.270
It set a really interesting precedent

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:29.020
throughout New York in
that because the seller

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.910
had not disclosed the
fact that it was actually

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:35.710
known to be haunted, whether
it was in fact, haunted or not.

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:37.210
The court, in that particular case,

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.450
took it as true that it was haunted.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:42.860
But the fact that it had
notoriety for being a ghost house

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:45.550
was something that the
seller should have disclosed

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:48.780
to the buyer and it allowed
the buyer to rescind the sale

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.320
and get out of buying that house.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.360
So sometimes, the existence of ghosts

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:55.630
is an important fact in trials.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.660
- Sounds like a pretty open-minded guy.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.270
- Yeah, they call him The Hammer.

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:01.536
- What can we do? It's all in
the hands of our lawyer now.

00:04:01.536 --> 00:04:03.582
- I think you guys are
making a big mistake.

00:04:03.582 --> 00:04:04.560
- Louis!

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.690
- I mostly do tax laws and
probate stuff occasionally.

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:09.651
I got my law degree at night school.

00:04:09.651 --> 00:04:11.400
- Well, that's fine, Louis.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:12.650
We got arrested at night.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:17.570
- Oh, I love it! Louis
Tully, the famous accountant

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:21.685
from Ghostbusters 1, who
obviously was turned into a dog

00:04:21.685 --> 00:04:25.520
and the Ghostbusters saved
him in that particular case,

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.870
went to law school at night,
which is a real thing.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.810
There are some law schools that allow you

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:32.560
to take night classes, it's
usually a four-year degree

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.080
instead of a three-year degree.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:37.540
That being said, you don't
wanna hire a tax lawyer

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.710
to handle your criminal arraignment.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:41.670
It's just not a good idea.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.100
Get someone who specializes
in criminal law.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.110
- Put these guys away fast and make sure

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:48.920
they go away for a long, long time, okay?

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:50.150
- I don't think it's gonna be hard

00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:51.820
with this list of charges.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.783
- Good. Very good.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:56.410
- What... what is going on here?

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:57.243
They haven't been arraigned.

00:04:57.243 --> 00:04:58.450
I assume they haven't been indicted.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:00.360
This isn't the actual
trial, they're not gonna be

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.923
tried and convicted in
this particular thing.

00:05:02.923 --> 00:05:06.880
I think that they were
arrested the night before

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:08.830
this particular hearing.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.680
There's no way they can be put
away for any amount of time

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.780
because this isn't the
place where that happens.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.250
You have to go through an entire process.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:17.270
The Ghostbusters need the discovery,

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:18.700
they need to know the evidence

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:21.210
that the prosecutors have against them.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:22.660
The only thing that's gonna happen here

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:24.640
is that the Ghostbusters
are gonna enter a plea

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:27.820
of not guilty and then
they'll be released on bail

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:30.890
'cause there's no reason to
put them in jail pending trial.

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:33.900
So nothing more is gonna
happen at this point.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.950
- Violating a judicial restraining order,

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:37.610
willful destruction of public property,

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:38.993
fraud, malicious mischief.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.310
See you in a couple of years

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:43.060
at your first parole hearing.

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:46.190
- So, okay. So apparently,
there was a restraining order

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:48.860
against the Ghostbusters,
given what happened

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.520
in the first Ghostbusters movie.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:51.540
That sort of makes sense.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:54.380
But the funny thing that the DA said here,

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:57.920
which probably most people are
not going to catch is that,

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:01.220
they are being indicted
for criminal mischief.

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:03.020
- [Devin] In New York,
tampering with someone's

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:05.780
public utilities is a violation

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:10.460
of the criminal mischief
statute under Section 145.15.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:12.210
It's criminal mischief
in the second degree.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:15.440
It is so funny that they
actually got the exact crime

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:16.273
for what they did here.

00:06:16.273 --> 00:06:18.580
Someone really did their research on this.

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:22.660
- Your Honor, ladies and
gentlemen of the audience.

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:24.533
- Jury? And there shouldn't be a jury.

00:06:24.533 --> 00:06:26.910
- I don't think it's fair
to call my clients frauds.

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:29.870
Okay, so the blackout was a big
problem for everybody, okay?

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:32.130
- Okay. It's crazy that
this is the criminal trial.

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.330
You see this a lot in dramas and comedies

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.650
where they just skip all
the procedural stuff.

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:39.510
But it really seems like they
skipped a whole bunch of stuff

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:40.790
and went straight to the trial.

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:42.730
Notwithstanding, Louis should probably

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:44.840
be talking to the jury,
if there is a jury present

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:47.300
at this time, and not to the judge.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.133
You guys know that.

00:06:48.133 --> 00:06:50.090
It's clear he's playing the fool here.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:53.110
He's an accountant! And
sometimes, he's the key master.

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:55.340
- Vinz Clortho, key master of Gozer.

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:59.010
- But he is absolutely not a
very good criminal attorney.

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:00.790
- I was stuck in an elevator for two hours

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:02.560
and I had to make the whole time.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.030
But I don't blame them!

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:06.650
'Cause one time I turned into
a dog and they helped me.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:07.624
Thank you.

00:07:07.624 --> 00:07:10.663
- (chuckles) Short but pointless.

00:07:13.858 --> 00:07:16.122
- Very good, Louis. Short but pointless.

00:07:16.122 --> 00:07:19.230
- (laughs) I know this
is a terrible movie,

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:22.520
but my friends and I will
quote this movie all the time.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:26.300
It's such an iconic version
of a criminal trial.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.360
Among lawyers, I think
this is right up there

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.080
with the Chewbacca Defense.

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:31.480
- [Prosecutor] Mr. Fianella,

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:36.653
please look at Exhibits A
through F on the table over here.

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:39.970
Do you recognize this equipment?

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:40.803
- [Mr. Fianella] Yeah.

00:07:40.803 --> 00:07:42.500
That's the stuff the cops
took from their truck.

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:43.333
- Okay.

00:07:43.333 --> 00:07:45.360
- Do you know what this
equipment is used for?

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.620
- I don't know.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.500
Catching ghosts, maybe? I dunno.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.620
- May I remind the court
that the defendants

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:53.040
are under a judicial restraining order

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.940
that strictly forbids them
from performing services

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:58.620
as paranormal investigators
or eliminators.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.790
- Okay, so a couple of
things are going on here

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:01.623
which is interesting.

00:08:01.623 --> 00:08:03.440
Number one, I suppose that she could ask

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:05.490
the question of the witness

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:08.170
whether he knows what these tools are for

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:09.810
and he can say that he doesn't know,

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:11.560
or that, I suppose his best guess is that

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:13.580
they are for hunting ghosts.

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:15.390
But because he's not a Ghostbuster,

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.850
assuming that Ghostbusting
is a real thing,

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:20.550
he doesn't have the
expert opinion necessary

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:22.190
to opine about those things.

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:24.130
He can absolutely testify
that those were the things

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:26.780
that were found at the scene of the crime,

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:29.780
but he probably is incapable
of offering an opinion

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:30.930
as to what they are.

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:33.830
Now, what this district attorney has done

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:36.673
is that she has taken this opportunity to

00:08:36.673 --> 00:08:39.950
lodge with the court, a copy
of the restraining order

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:41.883
that is against the Ghostbusters.

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:44.880
Arguably, it's sort of improper because

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.700
she's not asking a
question to the witness.

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:51.470
There are times to do this
sort of laying the foundation

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:53.970
but this is an issue of
law, not an issue of fact.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.960
So it's a little improper for her

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:58.933
to take the time now because
it's not the right time.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:02.075
- Now, Mr. Fianella,

00:09:02.075 --> 00:09:04.260
can you identify the substance in this jar

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:05.533
marked Exhibit F?

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:11.700
- Yeah. Yeah, that's the stuff, all right.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.450
Your Honor, I've been working underground

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:15.240
for Con Ed for 27 years.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.670
I never saw anything like this in my life.

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:18.920
- [Mr. Fianella] Whatever's down there,

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:19.990
they must have put it there.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:21.345
- No, we didn't!
- Objection.

00:09:21.345 --> 00:09:22.980
(gavel bangs)
- Shut up!

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:25.220
- So, if Louis totally was a good lawyer,

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:28.070
he absolutely would have
objected at that point

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:30.930
because well, again, this Con Ed worker,

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:34.590
could opine that during his
30 years working underground,

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:36.400
he's never seen anything like this.

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:38.890
It would be pure speculation
and that would be

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:40.900
the correct objection
to make, speculation.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.260
It would be speculation
for him to say that

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:45.160
it was the Ghostbusters that put it there.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:47.900
Just because he hasn't seen
it doesn't mean that he's seen

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:49.430
- [Devin] A hundred
percent of all the things

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:52.460
that are available beneath
the streets of Manhattan.

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:55.280
So if I was the attorney,
I would've objected.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:58.200
I would've moved to strike that testimony

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.020
that had just been elicited,
and I would've asked the judge

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:03.330
to give an instruction to
the jury that they are to

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.750
disregard that particular testimony

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.630
because it's totally improper.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:10.687
- So you were just trying
to help out a friend

00:10:10.687 --> 00:10:11.520
- Who was frightened

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:13.250
- who was scared of what
was happening to her,

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:15.200
- when you're scared
- Oh, I love this.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:17.870
- there was no evil intended, no malice,

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:19.640
because you live here and
when you live in a place

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:20.820
and you love it like you do

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.450
you don't want nothing bad to happen.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:23.820
What?
(Peter mumbles)

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:25.330
Because it'll never happen again,

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:26.650
it's an isolated incident,

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:27.730
it's a one shot deal.

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:29.020
- Objection, your honor!

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:30.603
- What?
- He's leading the witness.

00:10:30.603 --> 00:10:32.110
- Sustained!

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:34.810
- I'm sure that avid
watchers of this channel

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:36.280
will know what's going here.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.980
Again, this is played up
because it's totally improper.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:41.780
It's not that the lawyer
is leading the witness.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.687
It's that the witness
is leading the lawyer

00:10:44.687 --> 00:10:46.660
which is totally unnecessary.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.960
A leading question,
contrary to popular belief,

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:52.030
is just one that implies
the correct answer.

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:52.863
You're gonna ask

00:10:52.863 --> 00:10:55.550
a yes or no question and it's
still not considered leading

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:58.610
because you don't whether
it's a yes or no answer.

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:01.610
That being said, if you say
and imply that the answer

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:03.720
is yes, that can be leading.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:06.410
So, the way to get around
that is very, very simple.

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:08.620
You just simply ask, what happened?

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:11.600
What happened next? What did
you see? How did you feel?

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:15.490
These are open-ended questions
that would allow Louis

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:18.680
to allow Peter Venkman to just
give his side of the story.

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:20.720
That's really what direct examination is.

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:23.850
There's no reason for Louis
to be making a speech here.

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:26.840
He's not supposed to be
making any kind of statements,

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:28.110
it's supposed to be the witness.

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:30.850
And all he has to do is ask
Venkman what happened next

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:32.090
and why did you do this.

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:35.160
I think the writers of the
show know what they're doing

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:37.180
because it's so clearly ridiculous.

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:38.710
- [Prosecutor] I'll ask
you again, Dr. Venkman,

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:40.405
why were you digging the hole?

00:11:40.405 --> 00:11:43.010
And please remember you're under oath.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.230
- There are some things in this world

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:47.803
that go way beyond human understanding.

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:50.170
Things that cannot be explained.

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:53.100
Things that most people
don't wanna know about!

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:54.453
That is where we come in.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.060
- [Prosecutor] So what
you're saying is that

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:00.840
the world of the supernatural
is your exclusive province?

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:03.050
- And it's totally improper
for the district attorney

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:05.210
to walk to the jury and then

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:09.510
walk directly to the opposing witness,

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:10.830
especially who is a party.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:14.330
That bailiff, who is standing
right next to Peter Venkman,

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:17.020
should really intervene, and
get the district attorney

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:18.840
away from the witness.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.940
Both for the witness' safety,
so that the district attorney

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:23.080
doesn't attack him,

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:24.960
but also for the district
attorney's safety,

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:27.330
so that the witness doesn't attack her.

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:29.510
These things can happen
and there's no reason

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:31.070
for this district
attorney to be that close.

00:12:31.070 --> 00:12:33.580
It's totally improper and,
you know, things go bad,

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:36.600
the bailiff will tackle
one or both of them.

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:39.600
- Kitten, I think that
what I'm saying is that

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:41.770
sometimes, (bleep) happens,

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:43.350
someone has to deal with it,

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:44.875
and who ya gonna call?

00:12:44.875 --> 00:12:46.760
(crowd cheers)

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.470
- Okay, wait a minute. (laughs)

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:49.480
There's no jury!

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:51.930
- [Devin] You can see on the
far right hand corner that

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:54.260
there's no jury in the jury box.

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:55.290
Who are they

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.230
conducting this criminal trial for?

00:12:57.230 --> 00:12:58.820
- Peter Venkman, Raymond Stantz,

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:01.382
- [Judge] Egon Spengler, stand up!

00:13:01.382 --> 00:13:02.215
Get up!

00:13:04.226 --> 00:13:05.732
You too, Mr. Tully.

00:13:05.732 --> 00:13:08.203
(ominous music)

00:13:08.203 --> 00:13:10.298
Find you guilty on all charges!

00:13:10.298 --> 00:13:12.050
- (Devin scoffs) I think
that the judge here

00:13:12.050 --> 00:13:15.680
has said some things that
show some particular bias.

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:17.090
In California, at least,

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:20.820
when you get a judge that
you don't particularly like,

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:23.880
you are allowed one peremptory challenge.

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:26.770
- [Devin] It's called the
170.6, named after the statute.

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:29.710
If you know ahead of time
that the judge is The Hammer

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:32.420
and he doesn't believe in ghosts,

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:34.110
odds are you should
probably bounce that judge

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:35.530
and try to get another one.

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:36.840
Though you're sort of rolling the dice

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:39.460
that maybe the judge that
you get next is even worse.

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:40.760
- [Judge] I order you to pay fines

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:42.583
in the amount of $25,000 each!

00:13:43.517 --> 00:13:44.737
I sentence you to eighteen months

00:13:44.737 --> 00:13:47.303
in the city correctional
facility at Rikers Island!

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:50.720
- Wow, a year and a half in jail

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:53.700
for digging a hole in the road.

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:56.010
Well, I guess they
really did kinda screw up

00:13:56.010 --> 00:13:58.500
in terms of destroying
the public utilities

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.471
and causing a massive
blackout throughout the entire

00:14:00.471 --> 00:14:01.890
island of Manhattan.

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:03.700
Though interestingly, different varieties

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:06.000
of criminal mischief or criminal tampering

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:07.970
do carry with it different penalties

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:10.450
ranging from misdemeanor all the way up to

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:11.980
a class B felony.

00:14:11.980 --> 00:14:12.813
- Your honor?

00:14:12.813 --> 00:14:13.646
- Shut up!

00:14:13.646 --> 00:14:15.610
- [Judge] Tricksters like
you in decent society...

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:16.826
- Your honor, this is important.

00:14:16.826 --> 00:14:19.410
- [Judge] You prey upon the
gullibility of innocent people!

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:20.243
- Yes sir.

00:14:20.243 --> 00:14:21.350
- Be quiet.
- But...

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:22.916
- [Judge] If my hands were not tied

00:14:22.916 --> 00:14:25.281
by the unalterable fetters of the law,

00:14:25.281 --> 00:14:27.280
then I would indulge in the tradition

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:29.003
of our illustrious forbears,

00:14:29.003 --> 00:14:33.030
reach back to a purer, sterner justice,

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:34.805
and have you burned

00:14:34.805 --> 00:14:36.343
- (Devin mimicking the
Judge) at the stake!

00:14:37.492 --> 00:14:40.930
(Court attendees screaming)

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:42.020
- Wow!

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:45.155
- So, well, it is pretty
unusual for ghosts

00:14:45.155 --> 00:14:48.734
to be released as a
result of the sentencing.

00:14:48.734 --> 00:14:52.270
From time to time, judges do
like to hear themselves talk.

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:56.380
So right up until the ghosts
were released from the slime,

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:58.980
that could be something
that a judge would say

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:00.234
at the time of the sentencing.

00:15:00.234 --> 00:15:02.616
- The Scoleri Brothers!

00:15:02.616 --> 00:15:03.950
- Friends of yours?

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:07.238
- I tried them for murder.
Gave them the chair.

00:15:07.238 --> 00:15:09.678
(ghost screaming)

00:15:09.678 --> 00:15:11.585
- You gotta do something!

00:15:11.585 --> 00:15:14.065
- Why don't you just tell them
you don't believe in ghosts?

00:15:14.065 --> 00:15:16.398
(screaming)

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:22.410
- So while the Scoleri brother ghosts

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:23.670
are destroying this courtroom,

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:25.523
I guess now is a perfectly
good time to point out

00:15:25.523 --> 00:15:28.530
that this is a fairly realistic
courtroom for New York.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:31.520
I have practiced in the
Supreme Court of New York

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:35.290
and this would be a
particularly ornate courtroom

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:36.300
in the Supreme Court.

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:38.620
It's not totally dissimilar.

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.380
There would be, probably more paper,

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:42.290
there would be a lot more carpet,

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:45.030
this may be the ceremonial courtroom 1.

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:47.470
But that being said, this courtroom

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:48.690
that the ghosts are destroying -

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:49.770
pretty reasonable.

00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:52.940
And exactly the kind of
heavy, old wooden desks

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:54.450
you'd see for a counsel table

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:56.336
as they go flying across the room.

00:15:56.336 --> 00:15:57.940
(supernatural sounds)

00:15:57.940 --> 00:16:00.250
- You gotta do something! Help me!

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:02.031
- Don't talk to me, talk to my attorney.

00:16:02.031 --> 00:16:03.000
- And that's me!

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:05.660
My guys are still under a
judicial mistrangement order!

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:07.920
That blue thing I got from her!

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:09.847
- Oh god, I love that so much.

00:16:09.847 --> 00:16:11.460
(mimicking Louis) The
judicial mistrangement order!

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:13.000
That blue thing I got from her!

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:14.640
It used to be the case that you would get

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:18.520
motions and filings, it
would be called bluebacked.

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:20.630
- [Devin] I think that doesn't
really happen as much now

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:23.100
especially now that we've
gone to electronic files

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:24.080
for most of these things.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.470
But that being said, back in the day,

00:16:25.470 --> 00:16:28.220
you would absolutely have
certain pleadings and filings

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:31.040
that were bluebacked using blue paper.

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:33.260
- [Devin] And if you saw
earlier in this court scene,

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:35.550
the judicial restraining order

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:37.430
was actually covered in a blue back

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:39.280
which was probably accurate for the time.

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:41.480
- [Peter] You know it's
been a couple of years

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:42.730
since we used this stuff.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:44.820
Hope it still works.

00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:45.653
- [Egon] It should.

00:16:45.653 --> 00:16:48.050
Power cells have a
half-life of 5000 years.

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:50.490
- There's no time for a bench test!

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:51.492
Heat 'em up.

00:16:51.492 --> 00:16:54.263
- (sing-song) Doe, Ray, Egon!

00:16:54.263 --> 00:16:56.746
- (sing-song) Doe...

00:16:56.746 --> 00:16:57.746
- (sing-song) Ray...

00:16:59.158 --> 00:17:00.490
- (sing-song) Egon...

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:02.410
- I hate this shot right here.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:05.490
Ugh, where Egon looks... it's so weird.

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:07.430
It's weird the way he looks.

00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:10.263
(whimsical music)

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:12.153
- All right.

00:17:12.153 --> 00:17:14.560
Now it is time to give Ghostbusters 2

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:16.542
a grade for legal realism.

00:17:16.542 --> 00:17:18.778
(gavel bangs)

00:17:18.778 --> 00:17:20.570
- [Devin] So...

00:17:20.570 --> 00:17:22.760
God, I love this movie so much.

00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:24.570
I know the movie is not nearly as good

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:25.840
as the original Ghostbusters.

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:27.860
I will try and be objective.

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:29.630
But man, that's just a great scene.

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:30.463
It's just great.

00:17:30.463 --> 00:17:32.360
- [Devin] So on the one hand,
you have the Ghostbusters

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:34.640
dealing with the actual criminal code

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:36.510
that they probably
would've been charged with

00:17:36.510 --> 00:17:38.750
had this been a real-life event.

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:42.060
They were a hundred percent
guilty of criminal mischief

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:42.930
or criminal tampering.

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:45.660
So the writers got that absolutely right.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:47.050
- [Devin] And the events took place

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:49.840
at the correct courthouse,
the Supreme Court of New York

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:51.630
in a court room that
looks pretty reasonable

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:54.120
for what you'll see at the Supreme Court.

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:54.980
And it's possible

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:57.210
that the sentence that
they were about to receive

00:17:57.210 --> 00:18:00.550
before the Scoleri Brothers
were released was accurate.

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:03.530
That being said, the
timeline is completely wrong.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:07.610
They skipped over all of the
initial hearings and pleadings.

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:08.643
They were never arraigned,

00:18:08.643 --> 00:18:11.000
they never were released on bail,

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:12.780
- [Devin] the arguments that
were going back and forth

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:13.960
were totally wrong.

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:16.700
All of the courtroom proceedings were

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:19.380
totally incorrect,
including a lot of the bias

00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:21.730
that was shown at the sentencing.

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:23.397
So I'm going to give the courtroom scene

00:18:23.397 --> 00:18:24.860
- [Devin] and the release
of the Scoleri Brothers

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:27.260
in Ghostbusters 2 a flat C

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:29.320
that I'm going to raise to a C+

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:31.001
just because it is so darn quotable

00:18:31.001 --> 00:18:33.510
and so friggin' awesome.

